The '''2010–11 [[Venezuelan Primera División|Primera División]] season''' (officially the '''2010–11 Copa [[CANTV#Movilnet|Movilnet]]''' for sponsorship reasons) is the 29th professional season of [[Venezuela]]'s top-flight football league.

==Teams==
Eighteen teams will participate this season, sixteen of whom remain from the previous season. [[SD Centro Italo Venezolano|Centro Italo Venezolano]] and [[Llaneros de Guanare|Llaneros]] were relegated after accumulating the fewest points in the 2009–10 season aggregate table. They were replaced by [[Atlético Venezuela]] and [[Caroní FC|Caroní]], the 2009 Segunda División Apertura runner-up and 2010 Segunda División Clausura winner, respectively. In addition, Deportivo Italia changed their name to [[Deportivo Petare]] in the off-season. 
